bitrary Logarithm" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096835 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096835 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1039 "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096836 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1045 "Using Integration by Parts to Calculate Integrals With Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1050 1320.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "acc24286-334e-50b7-b51f-39796fa9c946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097056 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097056 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097056 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097056 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8f0b656-4bc9-55ad-bafd-83e444f61957" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097056 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(3x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1061 618388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e5d3fd98-fbd8-5b6d-a250-876573acf24e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1061 618389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "333f87c0-71a4-538e-9783-f364abf0caa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1061 618392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdfdcd42-ada8-5eea-ae27-e68cd87d7470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1061 618395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c0d6168f-5f91-5b54-9679-17a077751add" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.\n$$\n\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n\n$$\n\\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe usually let $u = x,$ but that would leave us with $v' = \\ln(x)$ which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our $u$ and $v'$ slightly differently, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{u}\\cdot {{x}_{⏟}}_{{v}^{′}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should *always* identify the logarithmic function with $u,$ not with $v'.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1065 897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "dbf22d18-c638-527f-a085-8fcc19fbfbeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257411 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+1)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257411 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257411 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47d0d172-5a30-57d5-a766-d99669bdec9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257525 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+2)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257525 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257525 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5650ea15-d618-5b47-8c28-c84f1b05c79b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257544 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921862575