db/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347738 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347738 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347738 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186346932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347738 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4e201519-7ef2-5188-bf15-bd65e9d10b4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348143 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348143 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348143 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348143 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int 9{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348143 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ded2d95-c1cd-581b-8bd9-c8df53884512" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348143 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\cdot (3{x}^{3})-\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348144 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348144 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348144 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348144 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348144 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9218e349-d846-5b44-8076-17797f61e65a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348144 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ {v}^{′}=25{x}^{4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\cdot (5{x}^{5})-\\int \\frac{5{x}^{5}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot {x}^{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{5}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424984 #edb/ref 1080 "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424984 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424984 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1fac7b1b